  "source_text": "Title: Loaded Baked Potato Soup with Crispy Skin Dippers\nServings: 4\n\nIngredients (component | amount unit | name | prep_style | pantry food_id):\n- Soup | 1500 g | potatoes |  | 000070\n- Soup | 150 g | bacon |  | 000630\n- Soup | 100 g | celery |  | 000117\n- Soup | 150 g | onion |  | 000111\n- Soup | 5 g | garlic |  | 000112\n- Soup | 625 ml | chicken fat (schmaltz) |  | 000389\n- Soup | 250 ml | whole milk |  | 000182\n- Soup | 250 ml | heavy cream |  | 000219\n- Soup | 100 g | cheddar |  | 000193\n- Soup | 30 ml | olive oil |  | 000378\n- Soup | 1 tsp | table salt |  | 000292\n- Soup | 0.5 tsp | ground black pepper |  | 000285\n- Crispy Potato Skin Dippers | 15 ml | olive oil |  | 000378\n- Crispy Potato Skin Dippers | 0.25 tsp | table salt |  | 000292\n- Crispy Potato Skin Dippers | 0.25 tsp | ground black pepper |  | 000285\n- Toppings | 100 ml | sour cream |  | 000222\n- Toppings | 5 g | chives |  | 000248\n- Toppings | 50 g | cheddar |  | 000193\n\nSteps in order (component | phase | minutes | text):\n1. Soup | Cook |  | Prick potatoes with a fork and coat in oil, salt, and pepper. Bake at 200°C for 1 hour or until soft.\n2. Crispy Potato Skin Dippers | Prep |  | Place the hollowed-out potato skins on a baking tray.\n3. Toppings | Prep |  | Dice the crispy bacon and finely chop the fresh chives.\n4. Soup | Cook |  | In a large pot, fry bacon slices until crispy. Remove the bacon and set aside, leaving the fat in the pot.\n5. Crispy Potato Skin Dippers | Cook |  | Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Bake at the oven's highest temperature for 5 minutes until very crispy.\n6. Toppings | Serve |  | Ladle soup into bowls. Top with extra cheddar, chopped bacon, a dollollop of sour cream, and chives. Serve with the skin dippers.\n7. Soup | Cook |  | Add celery, onion, and garlic to the rendered bacon fat. Sauté over medium heat until softened.\n8. Soup | Prep |  | Slice cooked potatoes, scoop out the centers, and add the potato flesh to the soup pot.\n9. Soup | Cook |  | Pour in chicken stock and half of the milk. Use an immersion blender to blitz until smooth.\n10. Soup | Cook |  | Stir in heavy cream and season with salt and pepper. Simmer gently.\n11. Soup | Cook |  | Turn off the heat and stir in the grated cheddar. Use the remaining milk to adjust the soup to your desired consistency.",
